      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Acknowledgements\nThis training manual is the result of the collaboration of the WHO Global Health Ethics Unit (GHE) in the \nDepartment of Knowledge, Ethics and Research (KER), the Department of Emergency Risk Management \nand Humanitarian Response (ERM) and the Department of Pandemic and Epidemic Diseases (PED). The \ndevelopment of this manual was led by Andreas Reis (GHE) with assistance from Abha Saxena, Coordinator \nGHE, and Jonathan Abrahams, ERM department.\nSpecial thanks go to Philippe Calain for overseeing the initial phase and design of the project and to Renaud \nBoulanger for coordinat",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Acknowledges the WHO units that produced the training manual and the staff who led it, noting it grew out of a 2009 WHO technical consultation on research ethics in epidemic response. It thanks chapter authors, publishers who allowed material to be reused, and many external reviewers. It also credits student workshops and 2015 pilot sessions in Guinea, Liberia and Sierra Leone that tested draft modules.",
