      "title": "Core competence 2: Ability to define adequate processes for ethics review in public health interventions, surveillance and research in emergencies",
      "pageStart": 53,
      "pageEnd": 55,
      "target": "../sections/sec-010-core-competence-2-ability-to-define-adequate-pro.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Ability to define adequate \nprocesses for ethics \nreview in public health \ninterventions, surveillance and \nresearch in emergencies\nSource: WHO\nSource: WHO\nCore competence 2: Ability to define adequate processes for ethics \nreview in public health interventions, surveillance and research in \nemergencies\nWhen ethics oversight is deemed necessary for public health activities, it is important that such oversight \nbe of high quality. The standard procedures that should be followed in the case of research are described in \nlearning objective 2.1. Learning objective 2.2 describes the circumstances i",
