        "text": "A training module on protecting privacy and confidentiality during emergencies. Its 90-minute session plan centres on a case in which a village leader asks a survey team for collected data, with suggested protective steps such as engaging leaders beforehand, avoiding identifiable data and transporting questionnaires in locked boxes. The background defines privacy and confidentiality and explains why emergencies threaten them, through less controlled settings, wider data sharing, improvised recording and limited resources for secure storage. It justifies the duty of confidentiality through beneficence, non-maleficence, autonomy and trustworthiness, and ends with references.",
